# Project Git Workflow

- Before starting new feature or bugfix work, assume an Issue should exist and be linked in the normal team workflow.
- Create new branches from the latest `main`.
- Branch names must use:
  - `feature/<description>` for feature work
  - `bugfix/<description>` for fixes
- Prefer multiple small commits over one very large commit.
- Keep review scope focused. Avoid submitting very large batches of unrelated files.
- Do not commit generated inputs, runtime data, logs, intermediate files, or large notebook outputs.
- Small test code and lightweight test fixtures are acceptable when they help verification.
- Commit messages should be concise and describe the change clearly.
- PRs should target `main`, link to the related Issue, explain the change, and include test evidence.
- Do not consider work complete until relevant tests or validation results are documented.
- Keep `main` stable and reviewable at all times.
